 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545775 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186545274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545775 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e5e29ad5-8429-5ccd-b63b-c47ea2c2bedf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545786 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186545313 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545786 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186545434 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545786 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186545510 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545786 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186545537 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545786 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186545567 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545786 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545786 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545786 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186545510 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545786 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f18a88f6-c880-5a4b-af7a-6a47ac397abd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545807 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186545715 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545807 #edb/ref 1069 "q-134849" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545807 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545807 #edb/ref 1071 "A submarine navigates part of the deep sea. The submarine starts at a high position relative to the bottom of the sea and submerges until it reaches a deeper position. Later it returns near to its starting level. The submarine's distance to the bottom of the sea relative to time can be described using a quadratic curve. Which of the following scatter plots corresponds to this situation?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545807 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "228f905a-60da-5b33-af12-e8ffff0a9be3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545807 #edb/ref 1074 "For a quantity that varies quadratically, the points on the plot should be scattered along a parabola.\n\nAmong the given options, the only scatter plot that fits the description is the following:\n\n![](images/5b/5b1d8d3c5e5661ca47cdba385b459491dffcb556cf38ab49cb092598763d057a.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545831 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186545744 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545831 #edb/ref 1069 "q-134850" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545831 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545831 #edb/ref 1071 "A new superhero movie is causing a stir. The number of views of its trailer has increased exponentially since it first launched. Which of the following scatter plots corresponds to this situation?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545831 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7decd470-9c6f-5eac-ae25-b28629130f6d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545831 #edb/ref 1074 "For an exponentially increasing quantity, the points should be scattered along a curve where the $y$-values increase rapidly.\n\nAmong the given options, the only scatter plot that fits the description is the following:\n\n![](images/42/4228c8bfe5e31be1692aad958c4c59e4c2ae9bc671545cc699dabe42a5d470dd.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545845 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186545724 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545845 #edb/ref 1069 "q-134880" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545845 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545845 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following scatter plots shows a possible negative linear dependence between $x$ and $y?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545845 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a3b544e1-6c2a-5c64-b0a2-84d40a5c487b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545845 #edb/ref 1074 "In the case of negative linear dependence, the points on the plot should be scattered along a line with a negative slope.\n\nAmong the given options, the only scatter plot that fits the description is the following:\n\n![](images/49/49578cc58c94128c3e77a36e14b67343dfcf8d402202736edbd802c673909b39.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545856 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186545786 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545856 #edb/ref 1069 "q-134889" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545856 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545856 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following scatter plots shows a possible exponential dependence between $x$ and $y?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545856 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "be65dc10-b369-5d8a-bd2f-a7251513d699" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545856 #edb/ref 1074 "In the case of exponential dependence, the points on the plot should be scattered along a curve whose $y$-values increase or decrease rapidly.\n\nAmong the given options, the only scatter plot that fits the description is the following:\n\n![](images/b4/b40de1f74b96a981e9588e63689a766fabef65f4c3f661ebf6f4d2c59e4cd3cc.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545865 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186545738 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545865 #edb/ref 1069 "q-17640" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545865 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545865 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/18/1862385f45f9082d3100246dbafd020c388c3fe4d83bc38e8c617916f79ab4a0.png)\n\nA drone is flying around some tourist buildings. The scatter plot above shows the correspondence between the drone's height, in meters, and the time, in minutes, since it started its journey. Which of the following is the most appropriate regression model for this data?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545865 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e2b9b16e-f138-5cec-b1bd-3819d0d7a9b5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545865 #edb/ref 1074 "As values of $x$ increase, the corresponding values of $y$ first increase and then decrease. It seems like the points on the plot are scattered along a parabola, as shown below.\n\n![](images/0a/0a00ddf1bea18a587a0a960a8965516a1cc3ff9ab9e13f25d6a23c59d51f44fc.png)\n\nTherefore, among the given options, the most appropriate regression model is *quadratic.*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545876 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186545775 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545876 #edb/ref 1069 "q-10763" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545876 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545876 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/76/7687bdd3945e1ad655a2be00e9d661c0e3916c49424d908ae2a314885e4fcc76.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above shows a correspondence between the variables $x$ and $y.$ Which of the following is the most appropriate regression model for this data?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545876 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fa22db6b-bdac-554c-ac94-acce50615822" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186545876 #edb/ref 1074 "As values of $x$ increase, the corresponding values of $y$ increase rapidly too. It seems like the points on the plot are scattered along an exponential curve, as shown below.\n\n![](images/4b/4bf51786207dbb75705d5e9406748e3a77c0cfe5a9e72144e6453bc7fb62bf3e.png)\n\nTherefore, among the given options, the most appropriate regression model is *exponential.*" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
